  "qualification_notes": [
    "An initial audio control used overlapping choices including SPEECH. Both cold bypasses chose SPEECH, so the semantic assertion failed before restore. Mutually exclusive song-title choices established a stable MARY_HAD_A_LITTLE_LAMB oracle; the failed controls are preserved.",
    "The first PP=1 fault rejected the incomplete client stream and restored the authenticated object, but vLLM omitted the child exit code from logs. The repeat used external strace restricted to exit_group and observed exit_group(70); no vLLM or connector code was modified.",
    "PP=2 long padded image and mixed cold controls stably answered OTHER. These paths prove deterministic complete-output equivalence plus authenticated rank payloads, not semantic classification accuracy; short image control was CATS. Negative experiments are retained.",
    "A remote PP stage exited 70 while the head health endpoint remained successful and the client hung. The final fault observation uses an external deployment-owned whole-group stop after observing worker exit. API readiness is false after that stop and the incomplete stream is rejected. No automatic cross-host supervisor or upstream readiness propagation is claimed."
  ],
